From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: meanaverage <meanaverage@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 10 Oct 2026 16:38:29 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] fix(svc): bound all static channel reassembly paths

Upstream's `SvcProcessor::max_message_size` (#2256) takes no limit unless a
processor sets one, and only DRDYNVC with Remote Credential Guard does. A
chunked message is as long as its first chunk declares, up to 4 GiB, and
is held until its last chunk arrives, so every other channel can be made
to hold that much.

The default is now 64 MiB (`DEFAULT_MAX_MESSAGE_SIZE`); `None` still takes
messages of any length. Clipboard takes up to 256 MiB, RDPSND and DRDYNVC
1 MiB (DRDYNVC's can still be set with `with_max_transport_message_size`).
Reassembly grows its buffer fallibly, up to the declared length or the
limit, and frees it when a sequence is dropped; an unfragmented message is
copied fallibly too. The capture replayer takes clipboard messages as long
as the live channel does.
